
==================== RUNNING trial-079 (esm2_t33_650M_aspect_prediction: health check for the 3-way aspect (C/F/P) classifier a real sequential-cascade first stage would need) ====================

note: trial-078 showed a decisive win from feeding the GROUND-TRUTH aspect into the depth-1 classifier, but that's an oracle upper bound - a real cascade needs an actual aspect predictor. Per user direction, before committing a full data/epoch budget to that predictor, this trial takes trial-071b (the original health-check trial for this model class: 3 epochs, 450 train (resampled)/100 val, batch_size=16, unfreeze_last_n=27, learning_rate=2e-5, weight_decay=0.2, output_dropout=0.2, bf16, --no-gradient-checkpointing) as the base and adapts it two ways: (1) 4 epochs instead of 3, with --max-train-samples reduced to 338 (450*3/4=337.5, rounded up) to hold the TOTAL training-examples budget constant (338*4=1352 vs the original 450*3=1350) while spreading it across more, smaller resampled draws; (2) --dataset-repo-id kelmoir/cafa6-aspect (generate_dataset_aspect.py) instead of the depth-1/coarse datasets - label space is just the 3 GO namespace roots. --batch-size 8 --grad-accum-steps 2 (effective batch 16) replaces trial-071b's flat batch_size=16. --checkpoint-mode final and --push-to-hub NOT set, matching trial-071b's own convention for a calibration trial.
